749e929d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10399" :question/id #uuid "39111b2a-0750-5a6c-9e79-aeb0c723d198" :question/math-academy-id "q-10399" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+1?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\nx\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+1,$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\ne n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & \\ne n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne n\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-10399/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd6703d2-36f6-5665-90e3-f75aea5f663b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10399"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-29438/selection/705e793be006111553be1736ac94d96b225c3c0c9d937d0607881921db66dd55" :answer/id #uuid "060cefe7-2b6a-5ca0-8c43-67072bae608e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29438/selection/7b0193b6e78da32fbd799f5188370c674770e0b65edc807646e1147ab62100d1" :answer/id #uuid "fd793fbf-6600-5951-855b-739aeef69ac8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29438/selection/86a69e1123cd49b8f47badb7db1c5f199c7da044b2e404fe99eab19a706ccc5a" :answer/id #uuid "b6cdcd2f-9dac-5fd3-9b0b-e40b0fa070d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29438/selection/88d5972af0cb